        "raw_output": "\n\nThe goal requires cooking all raw meat using the grill and serving all cooked meat on the plate in the serving area. Currently, raw_meat_1 is on the grill_side_area, and the grill_lid is closed, preventing access to the inside_grill. The plate is in the dish_rack, but it needs to be in the serving_area for serving.\n\nTo achieve the goal:\n1. The grill_lid must be opened to access the inside_grill.\n2. raw_meat_1 must be picked from the grill_side_area and placed inside the inside_grill.\n3. The grill_lid must be closed to cook the meat.\n4. The grill_lid must be opened again to access the cooked meat.\n5. The cooked meat must be picked and placed on the plate (in the plate_top region) while the plate is still in the dish_rack.\n6. The plate must then be picked from the dish_rack and placed in the serving_area to complete serving.\n\nThis sequence ensures the meat is cooked and served correctly. All preconditions for actions are satisfied:\n- Gripper is empty initially and after relevant actions.\n- Regions like inside_grill and plate_top are accessible when required.\n- Lid states (open/closed) are managed appropriately.\n\nFINAL ACTIONS:\nopen(grill_lid)\npick(raw_meat_1)\nplace(raw_meat_1, inside_grill)\nclose(grill_lid)\nopen(grill_lid)\npick(raw_meat_1)\nplace(raw_meat_1, plate_top)\npick(plate)\nplace(plate, serving_area)",
